1. Purpose & Scope:
This repository represents a non-commercial, academic, security research, and
reverse-engineering case study conducted exclusively by DDW-X under the doctrine
of Fair Use (17 U.S.C. § 107 and equivalent international fair dealing provisions).
The primary intent is scientific research, interoperability analysis, educational
instruction, and architectural benchmarking of WebGL2, WebAssembly, and 3D graphics
runtime pipelines.

2. Proprietary Assets & Trademarks:
All original client-side code, pre-compiled runtime assets, 3D CAD geometries,
trademarks, service marks, and trade dress associated with iJewel3D and its respective
affiliates remain the exclusive intellectual property of their original copyright
holders and creators. 

3. Researcher Contributions:
The MIT License applies strictly to the original analytical chapters, de-obfuscation
methodologies, architectural diagrams, diagnostics, mathematical reconstructions, and
custom auditing tools authored by DDW-X.
